 1 big thing: Guilfoyle out after misconduct reports 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Kimberly Guilfoyle in Athens last year. Photo: Aris Messinis/AFP via Getty Images Kimberly Guilfoyle has resigned as U.S. ambassador to Greece, Axios' Rebecca Falconer and Josephine Walker report. 

 Her exit follows Wall Street Journal reporting that she used her political connections to seek financial favors and promote private business interests. Guilfoyle has denied any wrongdoing.

 New White House press secretary Katie Zacharia told reporters today: "She has been a wonderful asset to the team and we wish her well." 🤳 Guilfoyle wrote on X : "My gratitude and respect for President Trump and Secretary [of State Marco] Rubio remain unwavering."

 "I am proud of what we accomplished together, and I will always be a loyal supporter of President Trump and his mission to Make America Great Again." White House press secretary Katie Zacharia conducts her debut briefing today. Photo: Kevin Lamarque/Reuters 📰 The Wall Street Journal reported last week that Guilfoyle allegedly sought $100,000 from a Trump donor to pay a credit card bill, and offered access to Trump administration officials in return.

 Guilfoyle's lawyer disputed the authenticity of messages quoted by the Journal. The U.S. Embassy in Athens said she has followed State Department ethics and gift-reporting guidelines. 👀 What we're watching: The State Department's inspector general is reviewing the allegations involving Guilfoyle, AP reports , citing an unnamed U.S. official.

