 2. 🪐 Off-world driving record 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Graphic: NASA NASA's Perseverance rover set a record for distance traveled on another planet or moon, the space agency says.

 The Mars rover hit 28.10 miles on Sunday, topping the Opportunity rover's previous record of 28.06 miles. 🧭 NASA credits the achievement to Perseverance's autonomous navigation system.

 The agency says: "The rover images the terrain while rolling, builds a 3D map of hazards, and plots its course between waypoints selected by rover planners on Earth — a capability the team calls 'thinking while driving.'" Perseverance took this image of its own tracks on Sunday. Photo: NASA/JPL-Caltech 🚀 Steven Lee, project manager of the Curiosity and Perseverance rovers at NASA's Jet Propulsion Laboratory, said: "The original mission called for no more than 12.4 miles of driving."

 "We've blown well past that, and with all mobility systems fully operational and favorable extended-ground-life test results, we expect Perseverance to keep adding to this record for many years to come." Go deeper ... Watch a video . 

 
 
