 4. 🏎️ 1 for the road: F1 returns to Africa 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 This new F1 track is planned near the new Kigali International Airport in Rwanda. Rendering: F1 Formula 1 is headed back to Africa for the first time since 1993, with Rwanda hosting a race in "the early 2030s." 

 The African Grand Prix will have a 10-year contract and take place at a track southeast of Rwanda's capital, Kigali. 🏁 Rwandan President Paul Kagame said at a launch event that he hopes the F1 event will "pave the way for other races to be hosted on the continent." 

